  "verbalization": "Ivosidenib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndromes Related To Topoisomerase Type 2 Inhibitor through a chain of indications involving Mitoxantrone. The drug is linked to Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia, Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome, and Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, all of which are classified under the broader category of Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndromes Related To Topoisomerase Type 2 Inhibitor. This suggests that Ivosidenib may influence the development or progression of these leukemias through a mechanism that involves Mitoxantrone, which is known to target topoisomerase type II. The shared indication with Mitoxantrone implies a potential overlap in therapeutic pathways or biological mechanisms, possibly through shared targets or downstream effects. The evidence supports a relationship where Ivosidenib may contribute to the pathogenesis of these conditions via a mechanism that involves Mitoxantrone, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
